questions on Instagram.

00:00:49.771 --> 00:00:52.741
Question number one:
"How did you guys meet?"

00:00:52.741 --> 00:00:56.074
- There was an unscripted-ish department

00:00:56.120 --> 00:00:57.560
at the time that you worked on,

00:00:57.560 --> 00:00:59.761
and somebody on that team was looking

00:00:59.761 --> 00:01:02.371
for a new, unscripted food show.

00:01:02.371 --> 00:01:04.243
And you were tasked
with coming up with this

00:01:04.243 --> 00:01:07.160
on-the-road, food, travel-ish show,

00:01:07.310 --> 00:01:08.640
like, city-guide show.

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:11.950
I was added to that show to help reduce,

00:01:11.950 --> 00:01:13.817
and like be a character on that.

00:01:13.817 --> 00:01:14.650
(beep)

00:01:14.650 --> 00:01:16.061
This sauce is incredible.

00:01:16.061 --> 00:01:17.380
- It's whimsical.

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:18.380
- Whimsical.

00:01:18.931 --> 00:01:20.211
- "Is a hot dog a sandwich?

00:01:20.211 --> 00:01:22.931
And what are your thoughts
on pineapple pizza?"

00:01:22.931 --> 00:01:24.042
- Is a hot dog a sandwich?

00:01:24.042 --> 00:01:24.875
- Yes.

00:01:24.875 --> 00:01:25.708
On three.

00:01:25.708 --> 00:01:27.041
One, two, three.

00:01:27.277 --> 00:01:28.110
- No.
- No.

00:01:28.110 --> 00:01:28.943
- Hey.

00:01:28.943 --> 00:01:30.026
Is a hot dog a sandwich?

00:01:30.026 --> 00:01:31.101
- Adam says no.

00:01:31.101 --> 00:01:33.291
- And what are your
thoughts on pineapple pizza?

00:01:33.291 --> 00:01:34.840
- Pro or negative on three.

00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:36.173
One, two, three.

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:37.363
- Pro.
- Okay.

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:39.320
(laughs)

00:01:39.320 --> 00:01:42.552
- @juliadural, "How do you
say Andrew's last name?"

00:01:42.552 --> 00:01:45.112
- So my last name looks hard to pronounce,

00:01:45.112 --> 00:01:47.120
but is actually very easy to pronounce.

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:48.370
It's Il-nik-ee.

00:01:48.491 --> 00:01:50.792
- "What was the most fun
Worth It video to film?"

00:01:50.792 --> 00:01:51.625
- Ooh.
- Ooh.

00:01:51.625 --> 00:01:52.458
- Ooh.

00:01:52.458 --> 00:01:53.291
- Ooh.

00:01:53.666 --> 00:01:54.912
You know what was really fun,

00:01:54.912 --> 00:01:57.232
is when we went to Seattle
to eat some salmon.

00:01:57.232 --> 00:02:00.400
'Cause we were just like
on a jolly road adventure.

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:01.861
It was like a fun, new place.

00:02:01.861 --> 00:02:04.279
I was blown away by the autumnal glory

00:02:04.279 --> 00:02:06.101
of the Pacific Northwest.

00:02:06.101 --> 00:02:08.301
- I would have to say sushi.

00:02:08.301 --> 00:02:10.051
Not part one, though.

00:02:10.160 --> 00:02:10.993
- Hmm.

00:02:10.993 --> 00:02:12.243
- Teaser alert.

00:02:12.380 --> 00:02:15.380
That's all I'm gonna say about that.

00:02:15.785 --> 00:02:18.560
- Not really a great food to talk through.

00:02:18.560 --> 00:02:19.731
- "Who else is on your team?

00:02:19.731 --> 00:02:21.432
I don't think you guys are mean enough

00:02:21.432 --> 00:02:23.091
to stick Adam with all the work."

00:02:23.091 --> 00:02:24.600
Great question, I'm glad you asked,

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:26.021
because over the years,

00:02:26.021 --> 00:02:27.978
we have had so many people who have

00:02:27.978 --> 00:02:29.991
contributed to the show in so many ways,

00:02:29.991 --> 00:02:32.752
that's just made Worth
It what it is today.

00:02:32.752 --> 00:02:35.811
- As you know, we make
this show here at Buzzfeed,

00:02:35.811 --> 00:02:37.441
where there's a ton of great people

00:02:37.441 --> 00:02:40.261
that help and support
us make what we make.

00:02:40.261 --> 00:02:41.441
Like there's a research team,

00:02:41.441 --> 00:02:42.952
that makes sure that we're factual.

00:02:42.952 --> 00:02:44.171
There's a legal team,

00:02:44.171 --> 00:02:47.395
that makes sure that
everything we do is legal,

00:02:47.395 --> 00:02:49.301
at least what you see on camera, hey-o.

00:02:49.301 --> 00:02:50.832
There's a production team,

00:02:50.832 --> 00:02:54.256
that helps with scheduling
and getting us places on time.

00:02:54.256 --> 00:02:56.691
A whole post-production support team.

00:02:56.691 --> 00:03:00.272
This season we have an extra
special additional person,

00:03:00.272 --> 00:03:01.105
who's name is Annie.

00:03:01.105 --> 00:03:03.891
You're gonna see her in
a bunch of the videos.

00:03:03.891 --> 00:03:04.731
(laughs)

00:03:04.731 --> 00:03:07.352
So if you ever hear that
trademark laugh in the background,

00:03:07.352 --> 00:03:09.112
you know who it's coming from.
- You know.

00:03:09.112 --> 00:03:10.381
- "What is the craziest
thing that happened

00:03:10.381 --> 00:03:11.940
off-camera that we haven't seen?"

00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:13.280
There's been some moments.

00:03:13.280 --> 00:03:17.363
- Yeah, there's one time (beep).

00:03:18.221 --> 00:03:20.291
And that is probably the worst thing

00:03:20.291 --> 00:03:21.124
that's happened on set.

00:03:21.124 --> 00:03:23.280
- "What happened to
the 1000 cinnamon rolls

00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:26.933
you owed Adam Bianchi on
the fried chicken episode?"

00:03:26.933 --> 00:03:28.792
- That wasn't our fried
chicken episode, that was a--

00:03:28.792 --> 00:03:30.709
- Game day foods, yeah.

00:03:30.731 --> 00:03:31.564
- Yeah.

00:03:31.564 --> 00:03:33.309
- Oh yeah, you owe Adam
1,000 cinnamon rolls.

00:03:33.309 --> 00:03:34.142
- I do.

00:03:34.142 --> 00:03:35.721
- Or one thousand dollar cinnamon roll.

00:03:35.721 --> 00:03:36.554
(beep)

00:03:36.554 --> 00:03:37.887
- Adam, if you finish that,

00:03:37.887 --> 00:03:40.221
I'll buy you a thousand
cinnamon rolls, if you eat that.

00:03:40.221 --> 00:03:43.691
I'm going to not give
him all 1,000 at once.

00:03:43.691 --> 00:03:45.858
I'm gonna kill him slowly.

00:03:46.312 --> 00:03:47.240
One at a time.

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:48.851
So it's starting today.

00:03:48.851 --> 00:03:51.101
- So how many have you given him?

00:03:51.101 --> 00:03:52.184
- Number one.

00:03:52.719 --> 00:03:56.719
This is me starting my
quest to pay off my debt.

00:03:57.341 --> 00:03:58.251
- That's one down.

00:03:58.251 --> 00:03:59.521
Put the ticker on the screen.

00:03:59.521 --> 00:04:02.464
We've eaten like ten dollars
worth of jam already.

00:04:02.464 --> 00:04:04.661
- "How does Andrew feel getting killed off

00:04:04.661 --> 00:04:06.040
by Ryan and Shane?"

00:04:06.040 --> 00:04:08.280
